Guard implementation:

```js
'use strict';
/**
 * Release-kicker guard helpers (gh-844, live incident 2026-10-10).
 * ...
 */

function pathsIgnoreFromWorkflow(yml) {
  var patterns = [];
  if (!yml) return patterns;
  var lines = yml.split(/\r?\n/);
  var inIgnore = false;
  for (var i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {
    var line = lines[i];
    var trimmed = line.trim();
    if (!inIgnore) {
      if (/^paths-ignore:\s*$/.test(trimmed)) { inIgnore = true; }
      continue;
    }
    // entries are '- 'pattern'' one indent level deeper
    var m = /^-\s*'([^']+)'\s*$/.exec(trimmed);
    if (m) { patterns.push(m[1]); continue; }
    // allow double quotes too
    var m2 = /^-\s*"([^"]+)"\s*$/.exec(trimmed);
    if (m2) { patterns.push(m2[1]); continue; }
    // any non-list line ends the block
    if (trimmed !== '' && trimmed.charAt(0) !== '#') break;
  }
  return patterns;
}
```

Wait — workflow yaml: paths-ignore block entries like `      - '.github/**'`. Entry lines start with `-`. A comment line `# CI-only changes...` is inside the block in the actual file. So: if line starts with `-`, parse; if comment/empty, continue; else break. Need to be careful about top-level `- cron:` elsewhere — but we stop at first non-entry, and paths-ignore block ends at `workflow_dispatch:` line. Good.

isIgnoredPath(file, patterns):
```js
function isIgnoredPath(file, patterns) {
  for (var i = 0; i < patterns.length; i++) {
    var p = patterns[i];
    if (p.slice(-3) === '/**') {
      if (file.indexOf(p.slice(0, -3) + '/') === 0) return true;
    } else if (file === p) {
      return true;
    }
  }
  return false;
}
```

filterRelevantFiles(files, patterns) → array filtered.

